      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <p class="mb-8 rounded-md border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-gray-900"><strong>Takes effect January 1, 2027.</strong> This is version 2.2 of the Buyer Terms. Until then, version 2.1 remains in effect: <a href="/legal/buyer-terms" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,45%)] underline">read version 2.1</a>.</p>

        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900">Buyer Terms</h1>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Effective Date:</strong> January 1, 2027 <strong>Version:</strong> 2.2</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">These Buyer Terms ("Terms") govern your participation as a Buyer on the BreederHQ Marketplace, including browsing listings, joining waitlists, paying reservation fees, purchasing animals, booking breeding services, and booking services from Service Providers. These Terms supplement and are incorporated into the BreederHQ Terms of Service, the Acceptable Use Policy, the Marketplace Transaction Terms, and the Legal Definitions Schedule.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">&gt; <strong>In plain terms: BreederHQ introduces you to sellers and service providers. It is not part of your deal.</strong> When you buy an animal, pay a deposit or reservation fee, or book a service, your agreement is with the breeder or service provider, not with BreederHQ. BreederHQ does not negotiate, set, approve, guarantee, or enforce the price, terms, conditions, warranties, health guarantees, deposits, reservation fees, refunds, delivery, or outcome of that agreement, and it is not a party to it. You and the seller or service provider own your transaction and every dispute about it. &gt; &gt; - <strong>Contracts.</strong> If your agreement is prepared or signed with BreederHQ's templates or signing tools, the seller or service provider and you choose its contents. A template is not legal advice and not a BreederHQ term. &gt; - <strong>Payments.</strong> Payments for your purchase or booking are made to the seller or service provider. BreederHQ does not hold your money in escrow and does not decide whether a refund is owed. &gt; - <strong>Disputes.</strong> BreederHQ has no duty to mediate or resolve a dispute between you and a seller or service provider. Any help it chooses to give is voluntary. To the extent the law allows, you release BreederHQ from claims arising from disputes with other users. The release has limits, including for BreederHQ's own wrongdoing and for rights the law does not let you give up, described in §4.4 of the Terms of Service. &gt; - <strong>The Identity Confirmed mark</strong> means only that one person passed a third-party ID check for the seller's account (§3.2). It is not BreederHQ's endorsement, and BreederHQ does not keep or give out the ID details from that check. &gt; &gt; This box is a summary. The rest of these Terms, and the documents they incorporate, control.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">"Buyer," "you," and "your" refer to any individual who browses, inquires about, reserves, or purchases animals or services through the BreederHQ Marketplace.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Version 2.2 of these Terms becomes binding on you only when the notice, effective-date, and affirmative-acceptance requirements in §12 are satisfied. Browsing, inquiring, reserving, purchasing, or otherwise taking part in a transaction does not by itself accept version 2.2.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Capitalized terms used in these Terms have the meanings given in the BreederHQ Legal Definitions Schedule, which is incorporated into these Terms by reference.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">2. Account Requirements</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.1 Registration</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">To participate in transactions on the Marketplace, you must create a BreederHQ account with accurate and current information. You must be at least 18 years of age (or the age of majority in your jurisdiction).</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.2 Accurate Information</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You agree to provide truthful information in your account profile, inquiries, and communications with Providers. Misrepresentation of your identity, intentions, or capacity to complete a transaction may result in account suspension or termination.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">3. Browsing, Inquiries, and Reliance</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.1 Listing Information; Credential Displays; Profile Indicators</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Listings on the Marketplace, including all descriptions, photos, health claims, pedigree data, service descriptions, pricing, and any credential displays, are created or attested by Providers, not by BreederHQ. Profile Indicators, badges, and other indicators displayed in connection with a Provider's profile or listing are created or attested by Providers, reflect facts about the Provider's account history on the Services, or display a passthrough result as described in §§2.4 to 2.6 of the Terms of Service (for example, the Identity Confirmed mark described in §3.2). <strong>BreederHQ does not verify, endorse, evaluate, validate, or guarantee the accuracy, authenticity, currency, or completeness of any such content. A passthrough display under §2.5 of the Terms of Service (Third-Party Registry Passthrough) or §2.6 of the Terms of Service (Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough) reports a third party's result; it is not BreederHQ's verification, endorsement, or warranty.</strong> BreederHQ does not open, read, or evaluate any document a Provider uploads in connection with a credential attestation; the act of BreederHQ displaying or linking to such a document is not a representation by BreederHQ as to the document's authenticity, currency, or contents.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.2 Due Diligence; Buyer Acknowledgment</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>You acknowledge and agree that BreederHQ has not conducted, and is under no obligation to conduct, any of the following due-diligence steps on your behalf with respect to any Provider, animal, or listing. You are solely responsible for conducting your own due diligence before entering into any transaction.</strong> Without limiting the foregoing, we strongly recommend that you:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Research the Provider's reputation, experience, and history;</li><li>Request and review health testing documentation and veterinary records;</li><li>Verify registration, pedigree, and credential claims through the relevant breed registry, issuing body, or licensing authority;</li><li>Ask the Provider detailed questions about the animal's history, temperament, and care, or about the scope and methods of any service to be rendered;</li><li>Arrange an in-person visit or live video call to see the animal or facility before purchase when possible;</li><li>Request and review the Provider's written contract, health guarantee, service agreement, and refund or cancellation policy before committing;</li><li>Consult your own veterinarian for guidance on health evaluations.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Where a Provider has uploaded a Supporting Document or has indicated holding a professional credential, license, or accreditation, <strong>you are responsible for independently confirming the credential with the issuing body</strong> before relying on it. The presence of a document link on the Services is not a substitute for that confirmation.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>The Identity Confirmed mark.</strong> Except for the older listings described below, before a Provider's listings, storefront, or services are published, the individual BreederHQ designates for the Provider's account must pass an identity check run by a third-party identity provider (currently Stripe Identity), as described in §2.6 of the Terms of Service. Where that individual passed, BreederHQ may show an Identity Confirmed mark on the Provider's profile and listings.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">&gt; <strong>In plain terms: what the Identity Confirmed mark means.</strong> The individual designated for the account that posted the listing (currently, the account's owner) passed the identity provider's check of a government photo ID and a live selfie, on the date shown with the mark where a date is shown. &gt; &gt; <strong>What it does not mean.</strong> It does not mean that BreederHQ checked the seller or service provider, their business name, licensing, or practices, or any animal. It does not mean that the person you are messaging or paying is the person who passed the check, or that the account has not changed hands since. BreederHQ does not vouch for any Provider because the mark is shown.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>A listing's presence on the Marketplace is not proof that its Provider passed the identity check.</strong> Some listings, storefronts, and services that were public before the requirement applied to them may remain public without the Identity Confirmed mark. BreederHQ does not offer any alternative to the identity check, as §2.6(e) of the Terms of Service states. Look for the mark itself, and do your own due diligence either way.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>BreederHQ cannot give you a seller's ID details.</strong> BreederHQ does not keep the ID document, the live photo, or the details read from them after the check's result is recorded; it keeps only whether the check passed, a reference number, and the date (§2.6(d) of the Terms of Service). BreederHQ cannot provide a seller's or service provider's ID, or the details from their identity check, to you, including if something goes wrong. The mark is not a way to identify, find, or pursue a seller, so get the information you need from the seller directly before you pay. The presence of the mark is not an endorsement, and its absence is not an accusation.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.3 Communication</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">All communications between you and Providers conducted through the BreederHQ messaging system are subject to the BreederHQ Terms of Service. You agree to communicate respectfully and in good faith.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.4 Provider Insurance and Licensing — Your Responsibility, Not BreederHQ's</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Where applicable to a Provider's profession or services (for example, a farrier, trainer, veterinarian, groomer, transporter, or pet sitter), the Provider may be required by applicable law to maintain professional licensing, insurance, or both. <strong>BreederHQ does not require, evaluate, verify, hold, broker, or facilitate any such licensing or insurance, and BreederHQ makes no representation that any Provider holds any such licensing or insurance.</strong> You are encouraged to confirm directly with the Provider, and with the applicable issuing body or insurance carrier, whether the Provider holds the licensing and insurance you consider necessary for your transaction. <strong>BreederHQ disclaims all liability for any harm arising from a Provider's lack of, lapse in, or misrepresentation of licensing or insurance, except to the extent caused by BreederHQ's own conduct, and subject to §4.3(c) and (d) of the Terms of Service.</strong> If you are a Consumer who lives in New Jersey, that last sentence does not apply to you; §10.5(b) of the Terms of Service applies instead.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">4. Waitlist Participation</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.1 Joining a Waitlist</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When you join a Provider's waitlist and pay a reservation fee, you are entering into a direct agreement with the Provider, not with BreederHQ. Before paying a reservation fee, you should:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Understand the Provider's reservation fee amount and what it covers;</li><li>Read and agree to the Provider's refund policy;</li><li>Understand the Provider's selection process and timeline;</li><li>Confirm whether the reservation fee is refundable, partially refundable, or non-refundable.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.2 Reservation Fee Payments</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A reservation fee is a payment obligation arising between you and the Provider, and is owed and payable to the Provider. Payment is collected at checkout by our third-party payment processor for the Provider. <strong>BreederHQ does not act as an escrow agent and does not hold reservation fees in trust for you or for the Provider. BreederHQ does not guarantee, insure, or backstop any reservation fee, and has no obligation to refund a reservation fee out of its own funds.</strong> Whether a refund is owed is governed by the Provider's stated refund policy and applicable law. <strong>The Provider is responsible for funding and authorizing any refund owed to you</strong>; where a refund is authorized, it is executed through the payment processor or, where a payment was routed through BreederHQ's payment infrastructure, through that infrastructure. <strong>Nothing in these Terms limits any right or remedy that cannot lawfully be waived, including any rights you may have under card network rules or against your card issuer.</strong></p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.3 Waitlist Position</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Your position on a waitlist is managed by the Provider. BreederHQ does not control or guarantee:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Your position on any waitlist;</li><li>The timeline for availability of animals;</li><li>The Provider's selection process or criteria;</li><li>That a suitable animal will be available for you.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.4 No Guarantee of Placement</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Joining a waitlist does not guarantee that you will receive an animal. Litter outcomes, Provider selection processes, and other factors may affect availability. If the Provider is unable to fulfill your reservation, the Provider's refund policy applies.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">5. Purchases</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.1 Direct Transaction</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">All purchases are direct transactions between you and the Provider. By completing a purchase, you agree to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Pay the agreed-upon price through the payment method provided;</li><li>Arrange and pay for transportation/delivery as agreed with the Provider;</li><li>Comply with all applicable laws regarding animal acquisition and transport in your jurisdiction;</li><li>Provide appropriate care for the animal upon receipt.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.2 Payment Processing</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Payments are processed by our third-party payment processor. By making a payment, you agree to the payment processor's terms of service. <strong>BreederHQ does not receive, hold, or have access to your payment card number or other card credentials.</strong> A payment for a purchase, reservation, or booking is made to the Provider. BreederHQ supplies the software through which the Provider requests and records it, and, where a payment is routed through BreederHQ's payment infrastructure, BreederHQ collects it only as the Provider's limited payments agent under §2.7 of the Terms of Service. BreederHQ's own role in payments is limited as described in §2.3 of the Terms of Service; it does not decide whether a payment, deposit, reservation fee, or refund is owed between you and a Provider.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.2A Taxes</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Prices shown are set by the Provider. Where tax applies to a transaction, it may be added to your total and will be shown at or before checkout when it is applied. <strong>If a price, total, or receipt does not show a tax line, or shows tax as zero, that does not mean no tax applies to your purchase.</strong></p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.3 Purchase Agreement</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">We strongly recommend that you obtain a written purchase agreement from the Provider that includes:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Complete description of the animal being purchased;</li><li>Total purchase price and payment terms;</li><li>Health guarantee terms and duration;</li><li>Spay/neuter requirements (if any);</li><li>Return and refund policy;</li><li>Registration transfer details;</li><li>Any other conditions or requirements.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Your agreement may be prepared or signed using BreederHQ's templates or tools. Those templates are starting points, not legal advice. Some contain sample terms, such as health-guarantee periods and limits on the seller's liability, that the Provider chose to keep, edit, and adopt as its own; they are not BreederHQ's terms (Terms of Service §7C.1). The law of your state, including laws that protect people who buy pets, may give you rights that your agreement cannot reduce or waive. The Provider remains responsible for the terms it prepares or sends. Read the complete agreement, check the information relating to your purchase, and obtain independent legal advice as needed before signing.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Terms of Service §7C governs these tools, including AI-assisted conversion and electronic signing. BreederHQ does not warrant that your agreement is legally adequate, valid, binding, or enforceable, and a signature record or PDF is not BreederHQ's certification of identity, authority, consent, or legal effect. The Provider and you choose and own the contents of your agreement; a template, including one BreederHQ provides, is not a term of BreederHQ's. BreederHQ does not become a party to your agreement by supplying these tools and does not undertake to enforce it or guarantee the outcome of a dispute over its wording, interpretation, or performance.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">These provisions are subject to the limitations and preserved rights in Terms of Service §§4.3, 7C.6, and 10.5 and apply prospectively as stated in §7C.7. They do not waive mandatory consumer protections, excuse the Provider's obligations, retroactively change an existing agreement, or make you responsible for the Provider's drafting. Consent to sign electronically is not, by itself, consent to electronic delivery of records that law requires to be provided to you in writing.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">6. Breeding Service Bookings and Service Provider Bookings</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">6.1 Service Agreement</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When booking a breeding service (stud service, semen purchase, etc.) or a service from a Service Provider (farrier, trainer, veterinarian, groomer, transporter, etc.), the terms of the service are between you and the Provider. Before booking, confirm:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Service type, scope, methods, pricing, and payment schedule;</li><li>For breeding services: breeding method (live cover, AI, shipped semen, etc.), return breeding or guarantee terms, required health testing and documentation;</li><li>For Service Provider bookings: the qualifications and experience of the individual(s) who will render the service, the service location, any limitations on service, and the Service Provider's cancellation and refund policy;</li><li>Timeline and scheduling details.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">6.2 Outcome Acknowledgment</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You acknowledge that:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Breeding outcomes (including conception, litter size, and offspring health) are inherently unpredictable; neither the Provider nor BreederHQ guarantees any specific breeding outcome;</li><li>Services rendered by Service Providers are subject to the inherent unpredictability of working with animals; outcomes (including animal response to training, treatment, transport, or grooming) cannot be guaranteed.</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">7. Refunds and Disputes</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.1 Provider Refund and Cancellation Policies</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Refund and cancellation terms for purchases, reservation fees, and services are established by each Provider. BreederHQ does not set, manage, or enforce Provider refund or cancellation policies.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.2 Resolving Disputes</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">If a dispute arises with a Provider, you should:</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">1. Contact the Provider directly to attempt resolution in good faith; 2. Document all communications and agreements; 3. If you believe fraud has occurred, report it to BreederHQ at <strong>legal@breederhq.com</strong>; 4. You may also contact your payment provider (bank or credit card company) to explore chargeback options if applicable.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.3 BreederHQ's Role</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ is not a party to your transaction and has no obligation to resolve disputes between you and a Provider. However, BreederHQ may:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Review fraud reports and take action against Provider accounts that violate platform policies;</li><li>Suspend display of a disputed credential pending the Provider's response under the procedure in §8.4 of the Acceptable Use Policy;</li><li>Provide transaction records upon request, subject to privacy considerations;</li><li>Suspend or remove Providers who demonstrate a pattern of bad faith conduct.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Any suspension-of-display or other action BreederHQ takes is an exercise of platform discretion in response to a credible report; it is not BreederHQ's adjudication of the underlying truth of any claim.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>No duty to mediate.</strong> BreederHQ has no duty to mediate, investigate, arbitrate, decide, or otherwise resolve any dispute between Users. Any help BreederHQ chooses to give, such as passing along a message, providing records it holds, or acting on a report, is voluntary, may stop at any time, does not make BreederHQ a party to the dispute, and creates no obligation to help again or to reach any particular outcome. Action BreederHQ takes to enforce its own User Agreements, such as removing a listing or suspending an account, is not a decision of a dispute between Users and does not affect their rights against each other.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.4 Disputes With BreederHQ</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">This Section 7 is about disputes between you and a Provider. A dispute between you and BreederHQ is governed by §10 of the Terms of Service. In summary, and subject to the full text of that Section: most disputes with BreederHQ are resolved by binding individual arbitration under the American Arbitration Association's consumer rules if you are a Consumer, with almost all arbitration fees paid by BreederHQ; where those rules allow, a dispute is decided on written submissions, any hearing is held by video or telephone, and an in-person hearing happens only if the arbitrator decides one is needed, in which case it is held in the county where you live, and either party, including BreederHQ, may still take part by video or telephone; either party may use small claims court instead; class actions are waived, except as stated in §10.3 of the Terms of Service; and you may opt out of arbitration by emailing legal@breederhq.com within 30 days after you first accept a version of the Terms of Service containing that opt-out, as described in §10.2(k) of the Terms of Service. These terms also cover a dispute with BreederHQ about something that happened before version 2.2 of the Terms of Service took effect for you, unless it was already filed in court or arbitration by then (§10.2(m) of the Terms of Service).</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.5 Release for Disputes Between Users</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">§4.4 of the Terms of Service, which also appears as §7.5 of the Marketplace Transaction Terms, contains your release of BreederHQ from claims arising from disputes between you and a Provider or another User, including the waiver of California Civil Code §1542, the claims and rights it does not cover, and how it applies to Consumers. It applies to you as a Buyer as stated there. It does not apply to you if you are a Consumer who lives in New Jersey.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">8. Buyer Responsibilities</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.1 Legal Compliance</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You are responsible for complying with all applicable laws in your jurisdiction regarding:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Animal ownership and possession;</li><li>Import/transport regulations (interstate or international);</li><li>Local zoning or housing restrictions for animals;</li><li>Species or breed-specific legislation;</li><li>Required permits, licenses, or registrations.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.2 Animal Welfare</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">By acquiring an animal through the Marketplace or by retaining a Service Provider to render services to an animal in your possession, you agree to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Provide appropriate food, water, shelter, veterinary care, and socialization;</li><li>Not use the animal for any illegal purpose, including animal fighting;</li><li>Comply with any contractual obligations agreed upon with the Provider (such as spay/neuter requirements or co-ownership terms).</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.3 Assumption of Risk</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You acknowledge and accept that:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Animals are living beings with inherent and unpredictable health and behavioral risks;</li><li>No amount of health testing, veterinary screening, or genetic analysis can guarantee the future health or temperament of an animal;</li><li>You assume all risks associated with animal ownership from the time you take possession;</li><li>You assume all risks associated with retaining a Service Provider to render services to an animal in your possession, including risks associated with the Service Provider's professional conduct, on-site safety, and the inherent risks of working with animals;</li><li>To the fullest extent permitted by law, BreederHQ has no liability for any injury, illness, death, property damage, or other loss related to an animal acquired through the Marketplace or to services rendered by a Provider engaged through the Marketplace.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">This Section does not limit BreederHQ's liability for its own fraud, willful misconduct, or gross negligence, or for death or personal injury caused by its own negligence, or any other liability preserved by §4.3(c) of the Terms of Service, or any right or remedy that cannot lawfully be waived. If you are a Consumer who lives in New Jersey, the statements in this Section that you assume risks and that BreederHQ has no liability do not apply to you; §10.5(b) of the Terms of Service applies instead.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">9. Prohibited Conduct</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You may NOT:</p>
